// KVFX Tools walkthrough: the voiceover script.
//
// One entry per voiceover file, found in assets/vo as <file>.wav (or .mp3), or
// under the name Higgsfield gave it, which contains `job`. `say` is exactly
// what the narrator reads; each "|" marks where an on-screen caption breaks
// (the narrator ignores it). The builder times every segment from its
// voiceover file, so a longer or shorter read simply stretches or shrinks that
// segment. `min` is the shortest the segment may be, in seconds, for when no
// voiceover file is there yet.
//
// Plain ES3 so After Effects can #include it, and Node can read it too.

var WT_SCRIPT = [
